BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Students for Life
DTSTART:20261020T230000
DTEND:20261021T000000
DTSTAMP:20260924T160042Z
UID:a2a899a80abab0c6c39c083f9976b2@worcester-colleges
DESCRIPTION:The Holy Cross chapter of Students for Life of America works t
 o foster increased concern and respect for human life. The group is concer
 ned with a broad range of life issues\, including abortion\, euthanasia\, 
 and capital punishment. We are committed to promoting dialogue on polarizi
 ng issues. The group meets regularly in Campion House to foster individual
  reflection\, to promote group community\, and to organize programs for th
 e wider campus community. --- Event Details: https://myhc.holycross.edu/rs
 vp?id=2154043\n\nSource: College of the Holy Cross\nEvent page: https://my
 hc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2154043
LOCATION:1 College Street\, Box 16A\, Worcester\, MA 01610\, United States
URL:https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2154043
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Take Back The Night
DTSTART:20261020T230000
DTEND:20261021T013000
DTSTAMP:20260924T160042Z
UID:2cb68e22e49b4638f57e33e773a4ed@worcester-colleges
DESCRIPTION:Take Back the Night is a community event where students\, facu
 lty\, and staff stand in solidarity with survivors of sexual violence and 
 affirm a shared commitment to a safer\, more supportive campus. The event 
 includes a peaceful march\, survivor stories\, and a guided reflection. Pa
 rticipants are welcome to support\, learn\, and share personal stories. St
 ories that are shared at this event will not initiate a Title IX report or
  investigation. If you would like to speak at TBTN\, read a piece (either 
 your own submission or an existing piece)\, and/or provide a testimony\, r
 eading\, poem\, song\, etc.\, please fill out this form. We appreciate you
 r interest and will send out more information as we approach the event. Pl
 ease let us know if you have any questions. Thank you. NOTE: As described 
 in the College’s Sexual Misconduct Policy\, public awareness events such
  as “Take Back the Night”\, candlelight vigils\, “survivor speak out
 s” and other public forms in which individuals disclose incidents of sex
 ual violence\, dating or domestic violence or stalking are NOT CONSIDERED 
 notice to the College adequate to trigger an obligation to investigate. Ho
 wever\, such events may inform the College’s prevention and education ef
 forts. Link to story: https://forms.gle/sf2xvmJCU3RmPqD97 Content warning:
  There will be discussion of sexual violence and survivor stories. --- Eve
 nt Details: https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2152236\n\nSource: College 
 of the Holy Cross\nEvent page: https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2152236
LOCATION:Hoval\, The College of the Holy Cross Hogan Campus Center- Suite 
 506\, Worcester\, MA 01610\, United States\, The College of the Holy Cross
 \, Hogan Campus Center- Suite 506\, Worcester\, MA 01610\, United States
URL:https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2152236
END:VEVENT
